 <P STYLE="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman" ALIGN="justify">(e) any fees or other charges that become due in connection with any
healthcare reform, change in government pricing or discounting schemes, or other action of a Governmental Authority, including that portion of the annual fee on prescription drug manufacturers imposed by the Patient Protection and Affordable Care
Act, Pub. L. <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">No.&nbsp;111-148</FONT> or similar sales-based fees adopted in the future, in each case, to the extent reasonably allocable to sales of the applicable product; and </P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman" ALIGN="justify">(f) amounts that are written off as uncollectible in accordance with the accounting procedures of the applicable Seller;
provided that if any such <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">written-off</FONT> amounts are subsequently collected, such collected amounts shall be included in Net Sales in the period in which they are subsequently collected. </P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman" ALIGN="justify">For the avoidance of doubt, if a single item falls into more than one of the categories set forth in clauses (a)-(f) above, such item may not
be deducted more than once. Unless otherwise specified herein, Net Sales shall be calculated in accordance with GAAP. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman" ALIGN="justify">Sales of the
